#: ../../src/loop.rst:63
msgid "Initializes the given `uv_loop_t` structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:69
msgid ""
"Set additional loop options.  You should normally call this before the "
"first call to :c:func:`uv_run` unless mentioned otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:72
msgid ""
"Returns 0 on success or a UV_E* error code on failure.  Be prepared to "
"handle UV_ENOSYS; it means the loop option is not supported by the "
"platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:75
msgid "Supported options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:77
msgid ""
"UV_LOOP_BLOCK_SIGNAL: Block a signal when polling for new events.  The "
"second argument to :c:func:`uv_loop_configure` is the signal number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:80
msgid ""
"This operation is currently only implemented for SIGPROF signals, to "
"suppress unnecessary wakeups when using a sampling profiler. Requesting "
"other signals will fail with UV_EINVAL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:84
msgid ""
"UV_METRICS_IDLE_TIME: Accumulate the amount of idle time the event loop "
"spends in the event provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:87
msgid "This option is necessary to use :c:func:`uv_metrics_idle_time`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:89
msgid ""
"UV_LOOP_USE_IO_URING_SQPOLL: Enable SQPOLL io_uring instance to handle "
"asynchronous file system operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:92
msgid "added the UV_METRICS_IDLE_TIME option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:94
msgid "added the UV_LOOP_USE_IO_URING_SQPOLL option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:98
msgid ""
"Releases all internal loop resources. Call this function only when the "
"loop has finished executing and all open handles and requests have been "
"closed, or it will return UV_EBUSY. After this function returns, the user"
" can free the memory allocated for the loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:105
msgid ""
"Returns the initialized default loop. It may return NULL in case of "
"allocation failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:108
msgid ""
"This function is just a convenient way for having a global loop "
"throughout an application, the default loop is in no way different than "
"the ones initialized with :c:func:`uv_loop_init`. As such, the default "
"loop can (and should) be closed with :c:func:`uv_loop_close` so the "
"resources associated with it are freed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:115
msgid "This function is not thread safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:119
msgid ""
"This function runs the event loop. It will act differently depending on "
"the specified mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:122
msgid ""
"UV_RUN_DEFAULT: Runs the event loop until there are no more active and "
"referenced handles or requests. Returns non-zero if :c:func:`uv_stop` was"
" called and there are still active handles or requests.  Returns zero in "
"all other cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:126
msgid ""
"UV_RUN_ONCE: Poll for i/o once. Note that this function blocks if there "
"are no pending callbacks. Returns zero when done (no active handles or "
"requests left), or non-zero if more callbacks are expected (meaning you "
"should run the event loop again sometime in the future)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:130
msgid ""
"UV_RUN_NOWAIT: Poll for i/o once but don't block if there are no pending "
"callbacks. Returns zero if done (no active handles or requests left), or "
"non-zero if more callbacks are expected (meaning you should run the event"
" loop again sometime in the future)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:135
msgid ":c:func:`uv_run` is not reentrant. It must not be called from a callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:139
msgid ""
"Returns non-zero if there are referenced active handles, active requests "
"or closing handles in the loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:144
msgid ""
"Stop the event loop, causing :c:func:`uv_run` to end as soon as possible."
" This will happen not sooner than the next loop iteration. If this "
"function was called before blocking for i/o, the loop won't block for i/o"
" on this iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:151
msgid ""
"Returns the size of the `uv_loop_t` structure. Useful for FFI binding "
"writers who don't want to know the structure layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:156
msgid ""
"Get backend file descriptor. Only kqueue, epoll and event ports are "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:159
msgid ""
"This can be used in conjunction with `uv_run(loop, UV_RUN_NOWAIT)` to "
"poll in one thread and run the event loop's callbacks in another see test"
"/test-embed.c for an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:164
msgid ""
"Embedding a kqueue fd in another kqueue pollset doesn't work on all "
"platforms. It's not an error to add the fd but it never generates events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:169
msgid ""
"Get the poll timeout. The return value is in milliseconds, or -1 for no "
"timeout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:174
msgid ""
"Return the current timestamp in milliseconds. The timestamp is cached at "
"the start of the event loop tick, see :c:func:`uv_update_time` for "
"details and rationale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:178
msgid ""
"The timestamp increases monotonically from some arbitrary point in time. "
"Don't make assumptions about the starting point, you will only get "
"disappointed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:183
msgid "Use :c:func:`uv_hrtime` if you need sub-millisecond granularity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:187
msgid ""
"Update the event loop's concept of \"now\". Libuv caches the current time"
" at the start of the event loop tick in order to reduce the number of "
"time-related system calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:191
msgid ""
"You won't normally need to call this function unless you have callbacks "
"that block the event loop for longer periods of time, where \"longer\" is"
" somewhat subjective but probably on the order of a millisecond or more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:197
msgid "Walk the list of handles: `walk_cb` will be executed with the given `arg`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:203
msgid ""
"Reinitialize any kernel state necessary in the child process after a "
":man:`fork(2)` system call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:206
msgid ""
"Previously started watchers will continue to be started in the child "
"process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:209
msgid ""
"It is necessary to explicitly call this function on every event loop "
"created in the parent process that you plan to continue to use in the "
"child, including the default loop (even if you don't continue to use it "
"in the parent). This function must be called before calling "
":c:func:`uv_run` or any other API function using the loop in the child. "
"Failure to do so will result in undefined behaviour, possibly including "
"duplicate events delivered to both parent and child or aborting the child"
" process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:218
msgid ""
"When possible, it is preferred to create a new loop in the child process "
"instead of reusing a loop created in the parent. New loops created in the"
" child process after the fork should not use this function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:223
msgid ""
"This function is not implemented on Windows, where it returns "
"``UV_ENOSYS``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:227
msgid ""
"This function is experimental. It may contain bugs, and is subject to "
"change or removal. API and ABI stability is not guaranteed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:232
msgid ""
"On Mac OS X, if directory FS event handles were in use in the parent "
"process *for any event loop*, the child process will no longer be able to"
" use the most efficient FSEvent implementation. Instead, uses of "
"directory FS event handles in the child will fall back to the same "
"implementation used for files and on other kqueue-based systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:241
msgid ""
"On AIX and SunOS, FS event handles that were already started in the "
"parent process at the time of forking will *not* deliver events in the "
"child process; they must be closed and restarted. On all other platforms,"
" they will continue to work normally without any further intervention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:249
msgid ""
"Any previous value returned from :c:func:`uv_backend_fd` is now invalid. "
"That function must be called again to determine the correct backend file "
"descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:255
msgid "Returns `loop->data`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/loop.rst:261
msgid "Sets `loop->data` to `data`."
msgstr ""

